TYPES.md §12.1 (DECISIONS 226), §8.3, §3.4: a method written in a variant body outside any case is checked like any method: `self` is the variant value (no E2108), no case field is in scope, and a case field read on `self` (typed `V`) is E3003 until narrowed; a result of the wrong type is E3002.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local variant Reward {
  item { count: Int }
  nothing

  fn total(self) -> Int { return self.count }

  fn bare(self) -> Int { return count }

  fn name(self) -> String { return 1 }

  fn me(self) -> Reward { return self }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3003]  a/a.canon:7:39
  a.Reward has no field count

error[E2102]  a/a.canon:9:33
  unknown name count (did you mean round?)

error[E3002]  a/a.canon:11:36
  expected String, found Int

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
